    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d993">

                <pb facs="1030" n="910" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg910"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00 Revolutions/135: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-03T21:00:00-05:00">March 3, 1931—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 4—2:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>87. My 81, March 2, 3 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d993-f1"/> Diplomatic corps at
                    meeting this morning decided to ignore Sanchez Cerro; to await notification from
                        <pb facs="1031" n="911" xml:id="pg911"/> Foreign Office as to composition
                    new junta before making any courtesy calls upon members of junta; and that
                    present transitory junta and provisional junta presently to be formed are
                    logical continuation of Sanchez Cerro government.</p>
                <p>Most of colleagues and I feel meeting premature and ill-considered. British and
                    Japanese state they wish to follow our lead regarding recognition.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
